IMPORT prelude

-- Human Biomedical Research Act 2015 (Singapore) -- what counts as human biomedical research and as human tissue (ss 2, 3, First
-- and Second Schedules), who gives consent for minors, adults lacking capacity and the dead (ss 7, 8, 11, 13(2)), withdrawing
-- consent (s 14), the deception defence (s 26(2)), paying for tissue (ss 32, 33), removing and using tissue (s 37(2), (3), (9)),
-- and the maximum penalties (ss 22(6), 26 to 33, 37 to 39, 50).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition (incorporating amendments up to 1 December 2021, in operation 31 December 2021), informal
-- consolidation, version in force from 5/12/2025, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/HBRA2015.txt. The latest amendment
-- in its legislative history is Act 19 of 2025 (Statutes (Miscellaneous Amendments) Act 2025), commencement 5 December 2025; the
-- body annotates Act 11 of 2023 (wef 01/05/2023) and Act 19 of 2025 (wef 05/12/2025).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0025 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to what a research subject, tissue donor, family member, researcher or tissue dealer meets.
-- Not encoded: administration (Part 2), institutional review boards (Part 4) beyond the waiver in s 13(2), research institutions'
-- duties and declarations (ss 23, 24), tissue banks (ss 34 to 36), codes of practice (Part 7), enforcement powers, prohibition
-- orders and inquiries (Part 8 other than s 50), appeals (Part 9), the Fifth Schedule waivers, s 8(1)(d) and s 10 (minors lacking
-- capacity, and tissue from minors), the "comparable effectiveness" condition for adults in s 7(1), the consent formalities in
-- s 6 and the information list in s 12.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Human Biomedical Research Act 2015 -- research and tissue`

§§ `2 -- adult and minor`

-- s 2: "adult" means "a person who is 21 years of age or older or a person below 21 years of age who was or is married";
-- "minor" means "a person who is below 21 years of age and who has never been married".
GIVEN `age in years` IS A NUMBER, `has ever married` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is an adult` IF
    `age in years` AT LEAST 21 OR `has ever married`

§§ `3 and Second Schedule -- what is human biomedical research`

-- s 3(2): research intended to study (a) "the prevention, prognostication, diagnosis or alleviation of any disease, disorder or
-- injury", (b) aesthetic appearance "through clinical procedures or techniques", or (c) "the performance or endurance of human
-- individuals", WHERE the research involves (d) an intervention with "a physical, mental or physiological effect", (e)
-- "individually-identifiable human biological material", or (f) "individually-identifiable health information".
-- s 3(3): ANY research involving human gametes or embryos, cytoplasmic hybrid embryos, human-animal combination embryos, or human
-- stem cells or neural cells introduced into an animal.
-- s 3(4) and Second Schedule: excluded -- 1, 2 normal psychology and intelligence studies at no more than minimal risk; 3 national
-- public health research (Infectious Diseases Act s 59A); 4 the National Registry of Diseases; 5 statistics under the Statistics
-- Act; 6 clinical trials of health products under the Health Products Act 2007; 7 clinical trials of medicinal products under the
-- Medicines Act 1975 (S 334/2019).
DECLARE Study HAS
    `studies disease, aesthetics or performance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves an intervention on the body` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses identifiable biological material` IS A BOOLEAN
    `uses identifiable health information` IS A BOOLEAN
    `involves gametes, embryos or human-animal combinations` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a clinical trial under the Health Products or Medicines Act` IS A BOOLEAN
    `studies normal psychology or intelligence at minimal risk` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is public health research, a registry or statistics` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the study` IS A Study
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the study is excluded by the Second Schedule` IF
        `the study`'s `is a clinical trial under the Health Products or Medicines Act`
    OR  `the study`'s `studies normal psychology or intelligence at minimal risk`
    OR  `the study`'s `is public health research, a registry or statistics`

GIVEN `the study` IS A Study
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the study is human biomedical research` IF
        (NOT `the study is excluded by the Second Schedule` `the study`)
    AND (    `the study`'s `involves gametes, embryos or human-animal combinations`
         OR  (    `the study`'s `studies disease, aesthetics or performance`
              AND (    `the study`'s `involves an intervention on the body`
                   OR  `the study`'s `uses identifiable biological material`
                   OR  `the study`'s `uses identifiable health information`)))

§§ `2 and First Schedule -- what is human tissue`

-- s 2: "human tissue" means "any human biological material but excludes human biological material specified in the First
-- Schedule". First Schedule: 1 "Hair shaft, cut without dermal hair root or follicle"; 2 "Nail plate, cut without underlying dermal
-- tissue"; 3 "Naturally excreted bodily fluids and waste products such as saliva, sweat, urine and faeces"; 4 material that is
-- "not individually-identifiable" AND substantially manipulated -- but NOT "merely" by cutting, grinding, centrifugation, freezing,
-- cryopreservation and the other methods listed in 4(2).
DECLARE Material IS ONE OF
    `a cut hair shaft without the root`
    `a plucked hair with its follicle`
    `a nail clipping`
    `saliva`
    `urine`
    `a blood sample`
    `a tumour biopsy`
    `anonymised cells substantially manipulated in culture`
    `anonymised tissue that has only been frozen`

GIVEN `the material` IS A Material
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the material is human tissue` IF
    CONSIDER `the material`
    WHEN `a cut hair shaft without the root` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a nail clipping` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `saliva` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `urine` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `anonymised cells substantially manipulated in culture` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `8 and 13(2) -- consent for a minor as a research subject`

-- s 8(1)(a): a minor with "sufficient understanding and intelligence" -- consent "from both the minor and at least one adult parent
-- or guardian"; (b) the minor alone where an IRB has waived the parent's consent under s 13(2); (c) a minor without sufficient
-- understanding -- one adult parent or guardian, where "there are reasonable grounds for believing that biomedical research of
-- comparable effectiveness cannot be carried out without the participation of the class of minors to which the minor belongs".
-- s 13(2) waiver: no more than minimal risk, rights and welfare not adversely affected, and not practicable without the waiver
-- (e.g. "neglected or abused minors", "adolescents in studies concerning treatment of sexually transmitted diseases").
-- (s 8(1)(d), minors lacking mental capacity, is not modelled.)
GIVEN `the minor understands` IS A BOOLEAN, `the minor consented` IS A BOOLEAN, `a parent consented` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `parental consent was waived` IS A BOOLEAN, `the research needs minors of this class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `consent for the minor is sufficient` IF
    IF `the minor understands`
    THEN `the minor consented` AND (`a parent consented` OR `parental consent was waived`)
    ELSE `a parent consented` AND `the research needs minors of this class`

§§ `7(1)(b) and 11(1) -- who consents for an adult lacking capacity, and for the dead`

-- s 7(1)(b) (no donee or deputy authorised): "in the order of priority stated, when persons in prior classes are not available": (i)
-- the spouse; (ii) an adult son or daughter; (iii) either parent or a guardian; (iv) an adult brother or sister; (v) "any other
-- person named by the adult as someone to be consulted". (A donee or deputy authorised to consent comes first: s 7(1)(a).)
-- s 11(1) (deceased person): (c) the spouse; (d) an adult son or daughter; (e) either parent or a guardian; (f) an adult brother or
-- sister; (g) "the administrator or executor of the estate"; (h) "any other person authorised or under obligation to dispose of
-- the body". Both: "in the absence of actual notice of contrary indications" by the person, "or actual notice of opposition of a
-- member of the same class or a prior class".
-- Rank 0 means the person is not in the list.
DECLARE Relative IS ONE OF
    `the spouse`
    `an adult son or daughter`
    `a parent or guardian`
    `an adult brother or sister`
    `a person the adult named to be consulted`
    `the executor or administrator`
    `the person bound to dispose of the body`

GIVEN `the relative` IS A Relative
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rank for an adult lacking capacity` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relative`
    WHEN `the spouse` THEN 1
    WHEN `an adult son or daughter` THEN 2
    WHEN `a parent or guardian` THEN 3
    WHEN `an adult brother or sister` THEN 4
    WHEN `a person the adult named to be consulted` THEN 5
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the relative` IS A Relative
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the rank for a deceased person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the relative`
    WHEN `the spouse` THEN 1
    WHEN `an adult son or daughter` THEN 2
    WHEN `a parent or guardian` THEN 3
    WHEN `an adult brother or sister` THEN 4
    WHEN `the executor or administrator` THEN 5
    WHEN `the person bound to dispose of the body` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 0

GIVEN `the relative` IS A Relative, `a higher class is available` IS A BOOLEAN, `the deceased objected` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the same or a prior class opposes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the relative may consent for the deceased` IF
        `the rank for a deceased person` `the relative` GREATER THAN 0
    AND (NOT `a higher class is available`)
    AND (NOT `the deceased objected`)
    AND (NOT `the same or a prior class opposes`)

§§ `14 -- withdrawal of consent`

-- s 14(1): a research subject may "at any time" withdraw consent to participation. (2): a tissue donor may withdraw consent to use
-- of the tissue for research if "(a) the tissue is individually-identifiable and has not been used for the research; or (b) ... has
-- been used for the research but it is practicable to discontinue further use". (3) information obtained before withdrawal "may be
-- retained and used". (4): "Any penalty or damages imposed solely by reason of the withdrawal ... is void and unenforceable."
GIVEN `the tissue is identifiable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the tissue has been used` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `discontinuing is practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the donor may withdraw consent` IF
    `the tissue is identifiable` AND ((NOT `the tissue has been used`) OR `discontinuing is practicable`)

§§ `26(1)(c) and (2) -- deceiving a person into research`

-- s 26(1)(c): causing a person "by means of deception or misrepresentation" to participate -- $100,000 or 10 years. (2): "It is a
-- defence ... if the defendant proves ALL of the following: (a) the deception or misrepresentation was a necessary requirement of
-- the human biomedical research; (b) the possibility of the deception or misrepresentation was disclosed to the research subject;
-- (c) the research was conducted in accordance with the research proposal approved by the reviewing authority."
GIVEN `the deception was necessary to the research` IS A BOOLEAN, `its possibility was disclosed` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the approved proposal was followed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deception defence is made out` IF
    `the deception was necessary to the research` AND `its possibility was disclosed` AND `the approved proposal was followed`

§§ `32 and 33 -- paying for human tissue`

-- s 32(1): a contract "for valuable consideration" for "the sale or supply of any human tissue from his or her body or from the body
-- of another person" is void; (2) entering into one -- $100,000 or 10 years; (3) giving, receiving, offering or negotiating
-- valuable consideration for another's tissue -- the same. (4) Not caught: (a) reimbursement of expenses necessarily incurred in
-- removal under other written law; (b) "any scheme introduced or approved by the Government granting medical benefits or privileges"
-- to a donor and family; (c) defraying costs of "removal, transportation, preparation, preservation, quality control or storage",
-- a living donor's "travel, accommodation, domestic help or child care" or "loss of earnings", and medical care or insurance.
-- s 33: no advertisement "relating to the buying or selling in Singapore of any human tissue" -- $100,000 or 10 years.
-- (s 32(6): ss 32 and 33 do not apply where the Human Organ Transplant Act 1987 ss 13, 14 or the Human Cloning and Other
-- Prohibited Practices Act 2004 s 13 applies -- organs, blood, eggs, sperm and embryos. Not modelled.)
DECLARE Arrangement IS ONE OF
    `selling one's own tissue for money`
    `paying another person for their tissue`
    `reimbursing a living donor's travel, child care and lost earnings`
    `paying for the storage and quality control of tissue`
    `a Government scheme of medical benefits for donors`
    `advertising to buy tissue in Singapore`

GIVEN `the arrangement` IS A Arrangement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the arrangement is an offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the arrangement`
    WHEN `reimbursing a living donor's travel, child care and lost earnings` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `paying for the storage and quality control of tissue` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Government scheme of medical benefits for donors` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `37(2), (3) and (9) -- removing and using tissue`

-- s 37(2): no removal of human tissue from an adult lacking mental capacity, a minor lacking mental capacity, or "a minor who lacks
-- sufficient understanding and intelligence to give consent" "unless the removal of the tissue was primarily for a therapeutic or
-- diagnostic purpose". (3) An IRB may waive that if "(a) the removal of the tissue involves no more than minimal risk" and "(b)
-- there are reasonable grounds for believing that the proposed areas of research cannot be carried out without the use of the
-- tissue from the class of persons". (9) Tissue removed for treatment may not be stored, supplied or used for research "unless the
-- medical practitioner or healthcare institution ... had completed all necessary therapeutic or diagnostic procedures and no longer
-- requires the tissue". (11): $50,000 or 5 years.
GIVEN `primarily therapeutic or diagnostic` IS A BOOLEAN, `the IRB waived that requirement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `tissue may be removed from a person unable to consent` IF
    `primarily therapeutic or diagnostic` OR `the IRB waived that requirement`

GIVEN `research consent was obtained` IS A BOOLEAN, `the treating doctor no longer needs it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `leftover clinical tissue may be used for research` IF
    `research consent was obtained` AND `the treating doctor no longer needs it`

§§ `22(6), 26 to 33, 37 to 39 and 50 -- maximum penalties`

-- s 22(6) research outside an institution, without IRB review or consent: "$50,000 or ... 5 years or to both"; s 26 compelling or
-- deceiving into research: $100,000 or 10 years; s 27(2) failing to safeguard identifiable information or material: $10,000 or 12
-- months; s 28(3) re-identifying anonymised information: $20,000 or 2 years; s 29(3) disclosing a research subject's information:
-- $20,000 or 2 years; s 30(2) prohibited research (Third Schedule): $100,000 or 10 years; s 31(4) restricted research: $100,000 or
-- 10 years; ss 32, 33 tissue trading and advertising: $100,000 or 10 years; s 37(11) tissue removal, storage, supply or use:
-- $50,000 or 5 years; s 38 compelling tissue donation: $100,000 or 10 years; s 39(3) disclosing a donor's information: $20,000 or
-- 2 years.
-- s 50: a body corporate convicted may be fined "not exceeding 2 times the maximum amount that the court could, but for this
-- section, impose as a fine for that offence".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `research without an institution, review or consent`
    `compelling or deceiving a person into research`
    `failing to safeguard identifiable data`
    `re-identifying anonymised data`
    `disclosing a research subject's information`
    `prohibited research`
    `restricted research outside the requirements`
    `trading in human tissue`
    `advertising human tissue for sale`
    `unlawful removal or use of tissue`
    `compelling a person to donate tissue`
    `disclosing a tissue donor's information`

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine for an individual` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `research without an institution, review or consent` THEN 50000
    WHEN `unlawful removal or use of tissue` THEN 50000
    WHEN `failing to safeguard identifiable data` THEN 10000
    WHEN `re-identifying anonymised data` THEN 20000
    WHEN `disclosing a research subject's information` THEN 20000
    WHEN `disclosing a tissue donor's information` THEN 20000
    OTHERWISE 100000

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `research without an institution, review or consent` THEN 60
    WHEN `unlawful removal or use of tissue` THEN 60
    WHEN `failing to safeguard identifiable data` THEN 12
    WHEN `re-identifying anonymised data` THEN 24
    WHEN `disclosing a research subject's information` THEN 24
    WHEN `disclosing a tissue donor's information` THEN 24
    OTHERWISE 120

GIVEN `the offence` IS A Offence, `convicted as a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `convicted as a body corporate`
    THEN `the maximum fine for an individual` `the offence` TIMES 2
    ELSE `the maximum fine for an individual` `the offence`
